Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 17 17:38:54 2026 +0000

    AnyList's comprises clause is live: the checker opens a type where-clause variable at a call, walk binds it at load, and AnyList's other operations move where the element type is known

    Climb batch 17, rung A (wip/rung-anylist-comprises, 920d23b08..b43dea24f), composed from the branch's net change. The team's library carried the clause as a comment on AnyList, "Not yet: comprises List[\E\] where [\E\]", and the specification's "Trait Declarations" lets a listed type hold a where-clause variable of the declaration at every value of it; the disambiguator, which both paths share, refused the variable ("E is undefined."), and the compiled checker refused four of AnyList's and the comprehension's calls, reading their arguments as a list of an unknown element type.

    Folded from the rung's record: FACTS F-251 added; ledger rows 751 to 758 (NEW-A-1 to NEW-A-8) added, their numbers put into Appendix I's entry "The traits that extend a closed trait"; PLAN, "Climb batch 17, listed for his review", A.worker.1, A.worker.2, A.skeptic.1 and A.skeptic.2, and A.worker.3 in item 13's third fork. The notes on rows 682, 701 and 307 were refused for length and are listed in the batch's RECORD.md. Row 636 closes after the rungs.

