commit 6d187d0697fd7298699459212fd5e6222064a0b9
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 17 17:41:34 2026 +0000

    Walk's load check reads every pair of generic declarations on its declared domains by the checker's rules, and refuses two whose declared domains are equal

    Climb batch 17, rung G (wip/rung-walk-generic-pairs, 8747b68cb..1481ddb0c), composed from the branch's net change with the skeptic's fix 36afa7eb1. The team's walk refused at load two generic declarations of one name unless some pair of their parameter types excluded each other, and read a type parameter as strictly below its bound, so it refused the specification's allowed pair ident[\T extends Shape\] beside ident[\T extends Round\] and loaded tie[\T extends Wide\](a: T, b: T) beside tie(a: Wide, b: Wide). The specification reads a declaration with static parameters over every instance within its bounds and states the No Duplicates, Return Type and Meet Rules on the declared domains (P-45).

    Folded from the rung's record: FACTS F-252 added, F-238, F-223 and F-155 rewritten; POSITIONS P-45's "Still to build" marked built; ledger row 759 (NEW-G-1) added, notes on rows 740, 741, 539 and 589; PLAN, "Climb batch 17, listed for his review", G.skeptic.1. The notes on rows 373 (closed) and 101 (full) were refused and are listed in the batch's RECORD.md, with row 589's claim. Rows 159, 742 and 549 close after the rungs.

    historical: ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/interpreter/evaluator/values/OverloadedFunction.java, Specification/advanced/overloading.tex, Specification/appendices/changes.tex

    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AmiXNpJxQ6TBwec4vJZHDB

